  1. Create the my-solana-project service account, with no login shell
     $ useradd --system --home /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project --shell /usr/sbin/nologin my-solana-project
  2. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/projects exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/projects
  3. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/deployments exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/deployments
  4. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/configs exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/configs
  5. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/logs exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/logs
  6. Ensure the platform directory /srv/solanaghana/systemd exists
     $ install -d -o root -g root -m 755 /srv/solanaghana/systemd
  7. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project exists, owned by my-solana-project
     $ install -d -o my-solana-project -g my-solana-project -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project
  8. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/deployments/my-solana-project exists, owned by my-solana-project
     $ install -d -o my-solana-project -g my-solana-project -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/deployments/my-solana-project
  9. Ensure /srv/solanaghana/logs/my-solana-project exists, owned by my-solana-project
     $ install -d -o my-solana-project -g my-solana-project -m 750 /srv/solanaghana/logs/my-solana-project
 10. Fetch the backend repository at main
     $ git clone --depth 1 --branch main https://github.com/user/backend /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/backend
 11. Build the backend
     $ cd /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/backend && npm run build
 12. Install the backend systemd unit
     $ install -o root -g root -m 644 /srv/solanaghana/systemd/my-solana-project-backend.service /etc/systemd/system/my-solana-project-backend.service
 13. Fetch the frontend repository at main
     $ git clone --depth 1 --branch main https://github.com/user/frontend /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/frontend
 14. Build the frontend
     $ cd /srv/solanaghana/projects/my-solana-project/frontend && npm run build
 15. Install the frontend systemd unit
     $ install -o root -g root -m 644 /srv/solanaghana/systemd/my-solana-project-frontend.service /etc/systemd/system/my-solana-project-frontend.service
 16. Reload systemd so the new units are visible
     $ systemctl daemon-reload
 17. Enable and start the backend
     $ systemctl enable --now my-solana-project-backend.service
 18. Enable and start the frontend
     $ systemctl enable --now my-solana-project-frontend.service
 19. Install the Caddy site configuration
     $ install -o root -g root -m 644 /srv/solanaghana/configs/my-solana-project.caddy /etc/caddy/sites/my-solana-project.caddy
 20. Reload Caddy, which provisions HTTPS for each new name
     $ systemctl reload caddy
 21. Point a DNS record for api.myproject.solanaghana.dev at this host, then it serves the backend
 22. Point a DNS record for myproject.solanaghana.dev at this host, then it serves the frontend
